{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types","id":1482295,"title":"So Predator types","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-29T15:28:42-07:00","id":1482295,"title":"So Predator types","content":"Several of the Predator types include flaws that don't seem like they would last long term.<br /> <br /> Bagger - the vampire kills the enemy, pays off the debt and then some, gains so much political power that the enemy becomes irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Blood Leech, Consensualist, Farmer - the vampire loses so much Humanity, perhaps even adopts a Path, so that any squeamishness about feeding from humans becomes silly.<br /> <br /> Siren - the vampire eats the spurned lover.<br /> <br /> How do you deal with this? Do you put an experience tax on them to pay off the flaw? Do you simply have the flaw evaporate once the situation has been dealt with in-character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T16:36:53-07:00","id":1482305,"title":"","content":"I am somewhat confused since I am not that familiar with v5. Why do you gain these flaws in the first place?<br /> <br /> It seems quite easy to cover up acts of your feeding if you have one of the common disciplines like obfuscate, presence, or dominate. Wont feeding from the homeless and other low income individuals be easy to do? The police are unlikely to investigate anything that happens to them since they are unlikely to be anyone important, and if you do kill them, dump the body in sewers and let the nosferatu have a bite. Or if you have animalism have your pets eat up the body. Or drop/bury the body in the forest or trash compactor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:07:53-07:00","id":1482325,"title":"","content":"At least for the Siren, I assume the enemy represented by the flaw is <i>this month's</i> spurned lover. You can deal with one specific individual in the short term, but your habitual feeding style is going to result in someone else taking their place soon enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T10:10:17-07:00","id":1482382,"title":"","content":"Two things about this. One, flaws don't go away as easily in v5. If you kill an enemy you'll develop a new one, for example. If you lose a flaw because of the story, you'll have to redistribute their dots into something else because of the sanctity of merits.<br /> <br /> Two, there are no raw ways to develop a path in v5. In addition, killing always provides a stain to humanity. That said, your odds of degeneration is extremely low at lower levels, but never 0.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482305#post1482305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems quite easy to cover up acts of your feeding if you have one of the common disciplines like obfuscate, presence, or dominate. Wont feeding from the homeless and other low income individuals be easy to do? The police are unlikely to investigate anything that happens to them since they are unlikely to be anyone important, and if you do kill them, dump the body in sewers and let the nosferatu have a bite. Or if you have animalism have your pets eat up the body. Or drop/bury the body in the forest or trash compactor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. A person going missing is just as bad as a finding a dead body. Depending on your city, and could eventually call the more serious law enforcement if it gets rampant enough. The methods we say can only get so far, and kindred are prone to mistakes.<br /> <br /> That said, if you're doing this to random strangers you're often in the clear. No one will link it to you, and being a vampire makes you practically immune to forensics. If you did this to a spured lover, then you're fucked! You have a connection to that person, and someone can put two and two together quickly if the lover goes missing. Same with people who publicly dislike you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T12:10:11-07:00","id":1482392,"title":"","content":"Flaws are supposed to help you create an interesting story, taking flaws just so you can work them off is contrary to their purpose. I'd allow players to work off some flaws, but always return them to a minimum of 3 or 2 eventually, either as the same flaw or a new one.<br /> <br /> It's why extra flaws for extra advantage points is no longer a thing at character creation, so that flaws are more meaningful.<br /> <br /> That said, I do allow more freedom when picking the flaws from predator types flaws <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482382#post1482382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two things about this. One, flaws don't go away as easily in v5. If you kill an enemy you'll develop a new one, for example. If you lose a flaw because of the story, you'll have to redistribute their dots into something else because of the sanctity of merits.<br /> <br /> Two, there are no raw ways to develop a path in v5. In addition, killing always provides a stain to humanity. That said, your odds of degeneration is extremely low at lower levels, but never 0.<br /> <br /> Yes and no. A person going missing is just as bad as a finding a dead body. Depending on your city, and could eventually call the more serious law enforcement if it gets rampant enough. The methods we say can only get so far, and kindred are prone to mistakes.<br /> <br /> That said, if you're doing this to random strangers you're often in the clear. No one will link it to you, and being a vampire makes you practically immune to forensics. If you did this to a spured lover, then you're fucked! You have a connection to that person, and someone can put two and two together quickly if the lover goes missing. Same with people who publicly dislike you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing doesn't necessarily provide a stain, depends on Tenets. <br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition is also a great adversary in these cases, too many unsolvable murders or disappearances is probably going to ping them as a possible vampire.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T13:27:37-07:00","id":1482401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482392#post1482392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Killing doesn't necessarily provide a stain, depends on Tenets.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition is also a great adversary in these cases, too many unsolvable murders or disappearances is probably going to ping them as a possible vampire.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's if someone reports that a homeless person or low income individual has gone missing, which even if they do, is unlikely to get any traction because of their economic status. If no one reports them, or the police in charge of investigating the cases ignore it, than the SI are unlikely to hear about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T13:49:24-07:00","id":1482402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482401#post1482401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's if someone reports that a homeless person or low income individual has gone missing, which even if they do, is unlikely to get any traction because of their economic status. If no one reports them, or the police in charge of investigating the cases ignore it, than the SI are unlikely to hear about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't consider a random homeless person enough for an Enemy flaw. Even if they don't have money, they must have some way of threatening the PCs or their plans, which will likely include a reason for them to be important or noticed if missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T14:05:34-07:00","id":1482404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482392#post1482392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing doesn't necessarily provide a stain, depends on Tenets.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition is also a great adversary in these cases, too many unsolvable murders or disappearances is probably going to ping them as a possible vampire.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All default Tenet types have some sin against murder, and the game by RAW assumes murder gives you stains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T15:32:00-07:00","id":1482412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482404#post1482404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All default Tenet types have some sin against murder, and the game by RAW assumes murder gives you stains.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it depends on the tenets? Because murder is not on the &quot;always gives stains&quot; list, unlike Embracing for example.<br /> <br /> The <b><i>sample </i></b>tenets all have stains for murder because that is a pretty basic ethic ground floor, though remember it is conditional on the Street Code. But if you pick &quot;Never snitch&quot;, &quot;Respect others, and demand respect&quot; and &quot;The guilty should suffer&quot;, murder doesn't give stains. <br /> <br /> I don't see where the game assumes that it gives you stains automatically either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T17:06:41-07:00","id":1482423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482412#post1482412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it depends on the tenets? Because murder is not on the &quot;always gives stains&quot; list, unlike Embracing for example.<br /> <br /> The <b><i>sample </i></b>tenets all have stains for murder because that is a pretty basic ethic ground floor, though remember it is conditional on the Street Code. But if you pick &quot;Never snitch&quot;, &quot;Respect others, and demand respect&quot; and &quot;The guilty should suffer&quot;, murder doesn't give stains.<br /> <br /> I don't see where the game assumes that it gives you stains automatically either.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Respect others, and demand respect</b>. How the actual fuck can you respect someone and then kill them?! Maybe if you go naturalist and say, &quot;I respect my prey&quot;, but even than the group as a whole has to agree to it. That's the thing about V5 Chronicle Tenets, they're like morality in general, subjective. That said, all the <b>sample tenet groups</b> all have some tenet that limits or prevents harm to another living thing in some way or another. The <b>Respect others</b> tenet is one of them specifically BTW. Can't justify respecting someone when you cause them suffering.<br /> <br /> It's from that perceptive that the designers likely desired Chronicle tenets to have some way to restrict murder and harm. As such the game itself assume murders, by default, gives stains. Yes, you can take the tenets and use them however you want, but the vast majority of players and STs make murder worthy of stains.<br /> <br /> BTW before anyone mentions it, yes even Gothic/Romantic tenets have a tenet that restricts harm and murder. It is <b>Uphold the norms of decent society</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T18:40:39-07:00","id":1482432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482423#post1482423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Respect others, and demand respect</b>. How the actual fuck can you respect someone and then kill them?! Maybe if you go naturalist and say, &quot;I respect my prey&quot;, but even than the group as a whole has to agree to it. That's the thing about V5 Chronicle Tenets, they're like morality in general, subjective. That said, all the <b>sample tenet groups</b> all have some tenet that limits or prevents harm to another living thing in some way or another. The <b>Respect others</b> tenet is one of them specifically BTW. Can't justify respecting someone when you cause them suffering.<br /> <br /> It's from that perceptive that the designers likely desired Chronicle tenets to have some way to restrict murder and harm. As such the game itself assume murders, by default, gives stains. Yes, you can take the tenets and use them however you want, but the vast majority of players and STs make murder worthy of stains.<br /> <br /> BTW before anyone mentions it, yes even Gothic/Romantic tenets have a tenet that restricts harm and murder. It is <b>Uphold the norms of decent society</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly as I said, it depends on the tenets. Of course, almost games will have a tenet that give it a stain, with conditions or not, because as the book says, they are there so that &quot;if the characters do become nihilistic serial killers, it carries a cost&quot;.<br /> <br /> More importantly, there is a list of things that always give stains, and murder is not on it.<br /> <br /> Obviously it can be assumed that cold-blooded murder will result in stains in most chronicles and it is the designer intent that they do, but there is an important distinction there. If you pick &quot;Reward success and punish Failure&quot;, &quot;Bend the mortal world to your will&quot; and &quot;Defend the Pack&quot; as the tenets for your chronicle, murdering your enemy won't bring stains, but embracing a mortal will still cause them. That is the important part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T01:12:07-07:00","id":1482467,"title":"","content":"Predator types are clearly one of the things of V5 where someone had a cool idea and nobody cared enough about how they executed it. <br /> The Character creation process has been made so difficult for the sake of balancing later XP expenditure and then... you throw a predator type in and that balance can go out the window. Setting all players to begin with 2/1/0 discipline spreads is a measure obviously taken for balance reasons, but when you can just +1 a discipline... the difference between 3/1/0 and 2/1/1 is a whole 10 xp. That's like, 10 sessions if you're using V5 xp rules and aren't abusing resonances or devouring vampires. <br /> <br /> <br /> That and I think most vampires are more opportunistic than strict on how they feed. The same strat every night is usually pretty unsustainable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T01:38:53-07:00","id":1482468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482467#post1482467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predator types are clearly one of the things of V5 where someone had a cool idea and nobody cared enough about how they executed it.<br /> The Character creation process has been made so difficult for the sake of balancing later XP expenditure and then... you throw a predator type in and that balance can go out the window. Setting all players to begin with 2/1/0 discipline spreads is a measure obviously taken for balance reasons, but when you can just +1 a discipline... the difference between 3/1/0 and 2/1/1 is a whole 10 xp. That's like, 10 sessions if you're using V5 xp rules and aren't abusing resonances or devouring vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> That and I think most vampires are more opportunistic than strict on how they feed. The same strat every night is usually pretty unsustainable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It is blatanty clear the 2/1/0 was a rule patch to avoid powergame. But, Just as not buying generation in previous editions could be considered a &quot;mistake&quot;, in v5 not using P.T. to buy the third point in a discipline IS a mistake as well, so I wonder why the writers didn't care. <br /> <br /> Maybe they thought that absolutely everyone would use p.t. to buy the third discipline point? They tried so hard to avoid powergame to the point of being restrictive enough to make chargen a pick in templates. But in the end there are objectively better options than others. 2/2/0 is a trap option and 2/1/1 is even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T05:41:36-07:00","id":1482484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482468#post1482468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they thought that absolutely everyone would use p.t. to buy the third discipline point? They tried so hard to avoid powergame to the point of being restrictive enough to make chargen a pick in templates. But in the end there are objectively better options than others. 2/2/0 is a trap option and 2/1/1 is even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole sticking to escalating XP costs was an error I thought they would avoid. Keeping it and then defeating the very template mechanic they built in to avoid abuse is just beyond me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T05:58:31-07:00","id":1482485,"title":"","content":"Do people even use the default xp rate anyway? All of the games I was in gave up to 5xp per session and I didn't see any power game issue at all to be honest, they could have just stuck with the old V20 rule that everybody seems to ignore, you know, the one that says that you can't increase anything more then 1 dot per story and it has to be justified in game, the whole template and predator type thing was unnecessary and only resulted in making character creation even longer and harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T07:14:54-07:00","id":1482488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482467#post1482467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and I think most vampires are more opportunistic than strict on how they feed. The same strat every night is usually pretty unsustainable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, which is why v5 says vampires usually don't hunt the same every night. Predator types best represent preferred hunting styles in most cases, and the back section on hunt does say most PTs don't force you to exclusively hunt as that Predator type.<br /> <br /> IDK why the PTs are in the game honestly, and I started with v5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482485#post1482485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people even use the default xp rate anyway? All of the games I was in gave up to 5xp per session and I didn't see any power game issue at all to be honest, they could have just stuck with the old V20 rule that everybody seems to ignore, you know, the one that says that you can't increase anything more then 1 dot per story and it has to be justified in game, the whole template and predator type thing was unnecessary and only resulted in making character creation even longer and harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone I played with did. One of the reasons I stopped playing v5. Hell as an ST that's what I did because of raw! I'm an ST that prefers to stick to the RaW as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Fun fact! V5 raw is insanely hard to even figure out some times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T08:04:57-07:00","id":1482491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482488#post1482488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, which is why v5 says vampires usually don't hunt the same every night. Predator types best represent preferred hunting styles in most cases, and the back section on hunt does say most PTs don't force you to exclusively hunt as that Predator type.<br /> <br /> IDK why the PTs are in the game honestly, and I started with v5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Everyone I played with did. One of the reasons I stopped playing v5. Hell as an ST that's what I did because of raw! I'm an ST that prefers to stick to the RaW as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Fun fact! V5 raw is insanely hard to even figure out some times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sticking with RAW with V5 will quickly kill what little enjoyment you might gain from it, especially the xp rate given that, since most people don't play more than once per week, it's going to take a whole year of game just to get a discipline to level 3, ALL of the games I was in used the old V20 xp rate, removed the power limit and when I asked if we could skip the Leslie Nielsen nonsense of vampire not seeing in the dark, I can't remember a single instance where I was denied it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T08:40:31-07:00","id":1482494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482488#post1482488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK why the PTs are in the game honestly, and I started with v5.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtM is about vampires. Vampires drink blood. They can do other things, but that's what vampires are. So I assume that the developers of this game about vampires decided that <i>how</i> they drink blood could be an significant topic.<br /> <br /> I find the idea of every vampire being a Lothario/succubus one night, then a cat burglar the next and then hunting deer utterly ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 05-31-2022, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T09:15:36-07:00","id":1482497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482494#post1482494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> VtM is about vampires. Vampires drink blood. They can do other things, but that's what vampires are. So I assume that the developers of this game about vampires decided that <i>how</i> they drink blood could be an significant topic.<br /> <br /> I find the idea of every vampire being a Lothario/succubus one night, then a cat burglar the next and then hunting deer utterly ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of a strawman description. A more likely scenario is a vampire who prefers to seduce prey in nightclubs, but when that fails she resorts to mugging hobos, and when that also fails, tries to grab rats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T09:39:54-07:00","id":1482499,"title":"","content":"RAW xp in v5 is a bit low, even when accounting from end of story XP. A base XP of 2, plus a little bonus when accomplishing some milestone or just doing a lot of progress on a session is much better. <hr />As for Preadtor types unbalance, I just change the free discipline dot to 15 XP you can spread on any discipline you can justify being useful for your hunting type. <br /> <br /> I do like them, think they are good for character building. Plus they are easy to homebrew without unbalancing stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T09:40:09-07:00","id":1482500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482494#post1482494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> VtM is about vampires. Vampires drink blood. They can do other things, but that's what vampires are. So I assume that the developers of this game about vampires decided that <i>how</i> they drink blood could be an significant topic.<br /> <br /> I find the idea of every vampire being a Lothario/succubus one night, then a cat burglar the next and then hunting deer utterly ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having a prefered way of feeding could have been better represented by merits and backgrounds also I find the idea of an immortal predator of the night deciding to stick with his prefered hunting habits during a time where they are actively being hunted down utterly ridiculous, a vampire who can't adapt is a dead vampire and tailoring a vampire skills toward a single feeding method is quickly going to spell trouble as soon the SI starts raiding your favourite hunting spots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T09:43:44-07:00","id":1482501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482497#post1482497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kind of a strawman description. A more likely scenario is a vampire who prefers to seduce prey in nightclubs, but when that fails she resorts to mugging hobos, and when that also fails, tries to grab rats.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a siren/scene queen. They have some skill that they routinely use to feed, in this case, by scoring. The RAW don't say that anybody who isn't an alleycat gets their arse handed to them or that rats will always slip away from non-farmers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482500#post1482500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a prefered way of feeding could have been better represented by merits and backgrounds</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Predator Types are. They get a discipline dot, a skill specialty, some sort of advantage in the form of a background, merit or humanity dot and usually a disadvantage along the same sort of lines. One discipline dot and speciality isn't even that big a difference by itself, so a character who primarily hunts by socialising could have a few dots of brawl and strength rather than just persuasion and charisma or whatever.<br /> <br /> Well, I suppose the discipline dot is big difference for the characters' purposes beyond feeding, but that because of the progressive xp cost that doesn't apply when choosing disciplines at character creation. I think that discipline costs should either be flattened or they should be removed from the Predator Type system. For example, I don't see how Fortitude helps consensualists, but it creates an incentive for players who want to use higher level Fortitude to choose that Predator Type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 05-31-2022, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:19:06-07:00","id":1482524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482485#post1482485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do people even use the default xp rate anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they do.<br /> <br /> Most STs will follow RAW on those things until they have enough experience with the role and with the game in question. Some will do that their whole lives, because some people are just like that.<br /> <br /> Around here I think most users have been playing for a long time, know more than one edition even if they started after V5 came out and talk with others about their experiences, so its probable most never saw reason to follow it. But for a lot of STs starting with V5 or with just the right mindset, the RAW is the way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482497#post1482497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's kind of a strawman description. A more likely scenario is a vampire who prefers to seduce prey in nightclubs, but when that fails she resorts to mugging hobos, and when that also fails, tries to grab rats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Predator Types may help to add some flavor to the game if done well, but you don't really need'em to address a hunter's methods. Your skill set naturally encourages some methods over others and personal preferences do the rest, but beggars can't be choosers, even in nature predators make compromises more often than not.<br /> <br /> And if the eventual thrill seeker likes to be a completely different hunter each night... well, what's the problem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482501#post1482501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what Predator Types are.</div> </div> </div> </div>And no one whatsoever is arguing that. You're trying to defend the concept while people are complaining about the rules given.<br /> <br /> &quot;Predator Types&quot; as a concept always existed within V:tM. Many common character concepts are just that or start of that way. Even the characters themselves recognize and name those habits since always, sometimes in a derogatory manner. Nothing new was added whatsoever except the rules backing it. And the problem is, those rules are bad.<br /> <br /> Those rules are bad because of another old problem of the game everyone here is keenly aware of: Creation Traps. Decisions that are linear during Character Creation, but affect affect a geometric growth rate after that, so in the end there are objectively optimal choices and others that will cost you in the long run.<br /> <br /> So, as they are now, the PT rules just mess with the balancing rules they put in place to address this problem, for little to no gain because what they're supposed to bring to the table already exists without them, so I don't blame anyone for not see a point in the rule in the first place.<br /> <br /> Oh, and yes, linear costs would be a lot better. Requiem 2nd Edition already does that and a lot of people already do that in their tables or want such rules, just don't feel confident to implement them themselves. Old news here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:31:02-07:00","id":1482527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482501#post1482501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a siren/scene queen. They have some skill that they routinely use to feed, in this case, by scoring. The RAW don't say that anybody who isn't an alleycat gets their arse handed to them or that rats will always slip away from non-farmers.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's what Predator Types are. They get a discipline dot, a skill specialty, some sort of advantage in the form of a background, merit or humanity dot and usually a disadvantage along the same sort of lines. One discipline dot and speciality isn't even that big a difference by itself, so a character who primarily hunts by socialising could have a few dots of brawl and strength rather than just persuasion and charisma or whatever.<br /> <br /> Well, I suppose the discipline dot is big difference for the characters' purposes beyond feeding, but that because of the progressive xp cost that doesn't apply when choosing disciplines at character creation. I think that discipline costs should either be flattened or they should be removed from the Predator Type system. For example, I don't see how Fortitude helps consensualists, but it creates an incentive for players who want to use higher level Fortitude to choose that Predator Type.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is not the way to do it, players should be free to build their characters the way they want, predators types are basically pregen character archetypes who make the choice for you and saddle you with pretty important flaws to boot, would it had been so difficult to imply let players chose these kinds of things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:33:23-07:00","id":1482529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482524#post1482524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course they do.<br /> <br /> Most STs will follow RAW on those things until they have enough experience with the role and with the game in question. Some will do that their whole lives, because some people are just like that.<br /> <br /> Around here I think most users have been playing for a long time, know more than one edition even if they started after V5 came out and talk with others about their experiences, so its probable most never saw reason to follow it. But for a lot of STs starting with V5 or with just the right mindset, the RAW is the way to go.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pretty much. Predator Types may help to add some flavor to the game if done well, but you don't really need'em to address a hunter's methods. Your skill set naturally encourages some methods over others and personal preferences do the rest, but beggars can't be choosers, even in nature predators make compromises more often than not.<br /> <br /> And if the eventual thrill seeker likes to be a completely different hunter each night... well, what's the problem?<br /> <br /> <br /> And no one whatsoever is arguing that. You're trying to defend the concept while people are complaining about the rules given.<br /> <br /> &quot;Predator Types&quot; as a concept always existed within V:tM. Many common character concepts are just that or start of that way. Even the characters themselves recognize and name those habits since always, sometimes in a derogatory manner. Nothing new was added whatsoever except the rules backing it. And the problem is, those rules are bad.<br /> <br /> Those rules are bad because of another old problem of the game everyone here is keenly aware of: Creation Traps. Decisions that are linear during Character Creation, but affect affect a geometric growth rate after that, so in the end there are objectively optimal choices and others that will cost you in the long run.<br /> <br /> So, as they are now, the PT rules just mess with the balancing rules they put in place to address this problem, for little to no gain because what they're supposed to bring to the table already exists without them, so I don't blame anyone for not see a point in the rule in the first place.<br /> <br /> Oh, and yes, linear costs would be a lot better. Requiem 2nd Edition already does that and a lot of people already do that in their tables or want such rules, just don't feel confident to implement them themselves. Old news here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have played V5 for a year since it came out, with many STs both vampire veterans and people who never even heard of the game before, never saw anyone actually use the normal xp rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T13:02:07-07:00","id":1482534,"title":"","content":"They could serve better as suggestions. Like classes in the middle Elder Scrolls games: you can choose one or you can build a custom class, but it's part of the character's design either way. V5 already proposes a sequence for choosing skills: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Think about what their occupation was in life and choose skills accordingly. A list of <i>Sample </i>Profession Packages is provided.</li> <li>Choose a couple of major life events from which they learnt skills. Another Sample list is there although this time, there's a suggestion to roll the dice to choose.</li> <li>As above but for hobbies.</li> <li>Choose some skills.</li> </ol><br /> A Predator Type could constitute one more step in that process. A list of defined Predator Types is simpler than asking players how their characters developed as predators. It's also more restrictive, but it shouldn't have to be. Maybe they want to be farmer with Celerity instead of Protean or Animalism. Maybe they don't want a built in enemy from their sex life; get them to take a third flaw dot instead. Maybe none of them fit, but they have an another idea; check that it's balanced and use that. Maybe they don't want to specify it at all; let them choose equivalent skills, backgrounds etc. instead and draw a dash in the box on their character sheet, but that doesn't mean that other players shouldn't have templates, if nothing more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T13:18:22-07:00","id":1482538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482534#post1482534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe they want to be farmer with Celerity instead of Protean or Animalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or how about this? They do want to be a Farmer, but someone who is a Farmer because they are an obsessive survivalist who thinks hunting humans is simply too great a risk to do routinely. Such a character would still have Animalism, but wouldn't have a Humanity 8 or feeding restriction. Instead, (s)he would have something like Obvious Predator, because they have completely cut themselves off from human contact and it has made them subtly creepy and weird. Wanting to be a Farmer shouldn't just assume two things about you linked to saintliness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T13:43:09-07:00","id":1482539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482534#post1482534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could serve better as suggestions. Like classes in the middle Elder Scrolls games: you can choose one or you can build a custom class, but it's part of the character's design either way. V5 already proposes a sequence for choosing skills:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Think about what their occupation was in life and choose skills accordingly. A list of <i>Sample </i>Profession Packages is provided.</li> <li>Choose a couple of major life events from which they learnt skills. Another Sample list is there although this time, there's a suggestion to roll the dice to choose.</li> <li>As above but for hobbies.</li> <li>Choose some skills.</li> </ol><br /> A Predator Type could constitute one more step in that process. A list of defined Predator Types is simpler than asking players how their characters developed as predators. It's also more restrictive, but it shouldn't have to be. Maybe they want to be farmer with Celerity instead of Protean or Animalism. Maybe they don't want a built in enemy from their sex life; get them to take a third flaw dot instead. Maybe none of them fit, but they have an another idea; check that it's balanced and use that. Maybe they don't want to specify it at all; let them choose equivalent skills, backgrounds etc. instead and draw a dash in the box on their character sheet, but that doesn't mean that other players shouldn't have templates, if nothing more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What you are proposing already existed in masquerade as far back as revised (don't know older editions) and it was as simple as allocating a freebie point, V5 forces predator types down your throat by default and doesn't offer you any alternative to that, why should I be forced to build my character over these templates? Your farmer with celerity is a good example, why should I take the base template and modify it when I could just have been given freebie points and built my character they way I actually wanted? Why do I have to starts with flaws that I never really chose? Instead of predator types they could have just gave players more starting freebie points to make their own characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T23:37:00-07:00","id":1482578,"title":"","content":"I personally think predator types are a really good idea, and fits the whole you are what you eat method. I do however agree that they missed a few aspects, and the difference between getting a level 1 discipline versus a level 3 is pretty hefty experience-wise, in particular as the game is rather stingy with experience in general. <br /> I would love to have seen a \u201chow to create your own predator type\u201d and then the list of examples. It is not impossible to shift around traits in one, but some people are a bit more RAW-leaning than others.<br /> Instead of a discipline, one idea would be to grant experience that must be used on disciplines (keeping the experience that cannot afford a new level)<br /> Another would be to list the (two?) resonances that would typically be acquired from this hunting, as a weighted tool for actual gameplay, but also it would give about two disciplines per resonance as choices. <br /> <br /> I think there is a lot of potential in the system that can already now be easily modified. Most of all, it feels right to me. <br /> And if you do not like it, the system is modular enough that compensating with 15-20 experience points would not break a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T03:03:46-07:00","id":1482583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482488#post1482488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, which is why v5 says vampires usually don't hunt the same every night. Predator types best represent preferred hunting styles in most cases, and the back section on hunt does say most PTs don't force you to exclusively hunt as that Predator type.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet half of the predator types include restrictive feeding type flaws/ <br /> Oh you eat animals? Vegan.<br /> You're a regular diablerist? Methuselah's thirst. <br /> Scene queen? Stick to that scene hard. <br /> Consentualist? Well you can't NOT have consent now can you? <br /> Bagger? Well there MUST be a reason you're afraid to go out on the street. <br /> <br /> Suddenly Cleavers seem like geniuses. <br /> But actually how valid is Cleaver as a distinct &quot;Predator type&quot;? Surely you'd go consentualist or sandman and just use your family on occasion, right? Unless you're living with the entire clan, you can't sustain yourself on spouse and three kids. <br /> <br /> I love the idea that hunting styles dictates your Disciplines but this is clearly not the way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T06:16:19-07:00","id":1482595,"title":"","content":"Predator Types as a bundle of traits (Specialty, Backgrounds, Merits and Disciplines, balanced with a Flaw) should just be a kind of grouped Advantage, like Paths in the StoryPath system.<br /> <br /> You could give them a simple mechanical or roleplaying bonus to make them slightly better than buying everything separately (e.g., +2 dice on hunting rolls or social rolls related to your Predator Type) or just have them as a time-saving device for those who want to make characters on the fly.<br /> <br /> Think of Concepts in Exalted Essence, for example, and how they suggest a certain set of traits for quick character creation, but don't force anything on you.<br /> <br /> The easiest fix, though, is flat XP costs. Then the third Discipline dot issue doesn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 06-01-2022, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T07:00:32-07:00","id":1482599,"title":"","content":"I think that the whole predator type is a solution for a problem that never existed in the first place, freebie points are a simple and elegant solution for this, the rest should be left to roleplay, you want your character to specialize in hunting animals? Get high survival and a haven in the middle of the woods, you like to seduce your prey? Drop a few freebie points on social attributes and skills, maybe get a merit to enhance your sex appeal, you are a bagger? Streetwise/larceny and contacts etc. I also hate that I'm forced to pick a flaw at character creation, like seriously why should players be forced into more problems when compulsions and banes are already a pain in the ass? If you have a concept that fit than sure, get enemy or hunted by the SI or whatever but it should always be a choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T07:19:21-07:00","id":1482602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types#post1482295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bagger - the vampire kills the enemy, pays off the debt and then some, gains so much political power that the enemy becomes irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, two points of Enemy flaw gives you an enemy with an effectiveness rating of four. That's a &quot;Deadly mortal, a Gifted mortal with magic or other supernatural powers, or a well-armed group of Gifted mortals (a private security squad, a lawyer contingent, a Russian mafia bratva)&quot; They're not minor.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just gain so much political power that they become irrelevant&quot; sounds simple but its like, &quot;Financial problems? Just become a millionaire, problem solved.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems like your issue is with the Flaw, not with the predator type. &quot;Just kill your enemy&quot; sounds simple enough but my brother in Caine, we are playing a roleplaying game. if that's the thing your character is trying to do then we are going to tell <i>a story</i> about that, it's not going to just happen in downtime between sessions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types#post1482295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Leech, Consensualist, Farmer - the vampire loses so much Humanity, perhaps even adopts a Path, so that any squeamishness about feeding from humans becomes silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all of these the flaw doesn't go away when you lose humanity. Prey exclusion gives you Stains if you violate the exclusion, regardless of what your humanity rating is. Farmer has a Willpower tax for drinking human blood, regardless of your humanity rating. Nothing about either of these flaws requires that the flaw is a conscious, deliberate moral choice. People (alive and dead) are complicated and trauma is complicated, even if you become a hardened evil asshole.<br /> <br /> But again it seems like your problem here is with the Flaw, not the Predator Type. &quot;Lol just lose enough humanity so your Flaw shouldn't matter&quot; is (1) not how the game rules work anyway, but mort importantly (2) a crappy way of engaging with the game's premise. If you're sitting at my table trying to figure out how to game around your character's weaknesses you won't be sitting at my table anymore because you're not a good fit for the kind of game I want to run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin","name":"Random Goblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T10:04:39-07:00","id":1482614,"title":"","content":"You're turning this into something personal. I'm not trying to &quot;game the system&quot;, I'm saying some of these flaws don't always make sense being permanent, and that there should be some game-mechanic to represent that potential impermanence. Whether you approve of me as an individual is completely irrelevant to this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T10:23:19-07:00","id":1482616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482614#post1482614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're turning this into something personal. I'm not trying to &quot;game the system&quot;, I'm saying some of these flaws don't always make sense being permanent, and that there should be some game-mechanic to represent that potential impermanence. Whether you approve of me as an individual is completely irrelevant to this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was using the generic you, not specifically you CajunKhan <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generic_you\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generic_you</a>. But I do think if a player is looking for holes to exploit in the system, then they are not approaching the game in a way that would be welcome at my table.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think the issue is this: if a Flaw can be easily circumvented, it's not a real Flaw that has points on your character sheet. Or the converse, if you pick an option in character generation that gives you a Flaw, it can't be something that's easy to circumvent. If you have an Enemy, it needs to be an enemy that isn't able to be trivially dealt with. If you want to go after your Enemy, that's great, I would love that as your ST, let's make a whole story about that. But it's going to be <i>a whole story</i>.<br /> <br /> There's a sidebar in the corebook about gaining and losing Advantages that goes into this. Although it focuses on losing Backgrounds (your Haven can burn down, your Retainer can die), it mentions Flaws and seems to be equally applicable. Tons of advantages and flaws are potentially impermanent. But there's a game happening at the same time as a story: if you off your Enemy, a new one will eventually come along for the same reasons as you had the old one, unless you are prepared to pay an appropriate cost, because otherwise you got something for nothing in a way that isn't really fair to other players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27061,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin","user":"Random Goblin","date":". 06-01-2022, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27061-random-goblin","name":"Random Goblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T10:55:27-07:00","id":1482617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482616#post1482616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> unless you are prepared to pay an appropriate cost, because otherwise you got something for nothing in a way that isn't really fair to other players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am willing to pay an appropriate cost. There just is no game mechanic to pay the cost for flaws. That's my point. There should be a game mechanic to buy off flaws that no longer make sense for the character. Right now there is no such game mechanic. If you start as a siren, and your character switches to farmer because they are trying to achieve golconda, and goes off to live in a cave, somehow they still have the spurned lover flaw until the end of time according to current mechanics. If you're a Farmer, you gradually lose humanity over the course of the story and drop to humanity 3, somehow you still have the feeding restriction and can never buy it off until the end of time. I am not arguing for there to be no price. I am arguing for a price mechanic to exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482616#post1482616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it mentions Flaws and seems to be equally applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mechanically it's not. There is no mechanism for buying off flaws.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-01-2022, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:08:10-07:00","id":1482619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random Goblin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482616#post1482616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was using the generic you, not specifically you CajunKhan <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generic_you\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generic_you</a>. But I do think if a player is looking for holes to exploit in the system, then they are not approaching the game in a way that would be welcome at my table.<br /> <br /> Anyway I think the issue is this: if a Flaw can be easily circumvented, it's not a real Flaw that has points on your character sheet. Or the converse, if you pick an option in character generation that gives you a Flaw, it can't be something that's easy to circumvent. If you have an Enemy, it needs to be an enemy that isn't able to be trivially dealt with. If you want to go after your Enemy, that's great, I would love that as your ST, let's make a whole story about that. But it's going to be <i>a whole story</i>.<br /> <br /> There's a sidebar in the corebook about gaining and losing Advantages that goes into this. Although it focuses on losing Backgrounds (your Haven can burn down, your Retainer can die), it mentions Flaws and seems to be equally applicable. Tons of advantages and flaws are potentially impermanent. But there's a game happening at the same time as a story: if you off your Enemy, a new one will eventually come along for the same reasons as you had the old one, unless you are prepared to pay an appropriate cost, because otherwise you got something for nothing in a way that isn't really fair to other players.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends from the flaws you get, butchering a gang that is pestering you shouldn't be that much of a problem even for a V5 vamp, humans are still humans and if an ST would had me go through the rolls and switch the flaw for another one, I would leave that table instantly because that tells me that the ST is going to invalidate my character's choices and just railroad me into the rest of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:17:40-07:00","id":1482622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482619#post1482619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Depends from the flaws you get, butchering a gang that is pestering you shouldn't be that much of a problem even for a V5 vamp, humans are still humans and if an ST would had me go through the rolls and switch the flaw for another one, I would leave that table instantly because that tells me that the ST is going to invalidate my character's choices and just railroad me into the rest of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a compromise where you pay as much to buy off the flaw as you would for the same dots worth of backgrounds?<br /> <br /> I mean picture this: you take Siren, and there's this person who tracks you to the only nightclubs you can get permission to hunt at and constantly makes a scene. Perfectly reasonable flaw for a beginning character. Over the course of a year of play, your character loses humanity, and becomes more brutal, deciding that seducing people is more work than its worth and just starts mugging hobos. Does the person who was making a scene in nightclubs start tracking you to alleyways and making a scene while you punch hobos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-01-2022, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:24:47-07:00","id":1482634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482622#post1482622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about a compromise where you pay as much to buy off the flaw as you would for the same dots worth of backgrounds?<br /> <br /> I mean picture this: you take Siren, and there's this person who tracks you to the only nightclubs you can get permission to hunt at and constantly makes a scene. Perfectly reasonable flaw for a beginning character. Over the course of a year of play, your character loses humanity, and becomes more brutal, deciding that seducing people is more work than its worth and just starts mugging hobos. Does the person who was making a scene in nightclubs start tracking you to alleyways and making a scene while you punch hobos?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would prefer to do it the way it was done in V20, you work out your flaws in game, weather they can easily solved or not, it will depend from the story, I really don't like this bargaining thing of getting something for something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T14:06:33-07:00","id":1482654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482599#post1482599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the whole predator type is a solution for a problem that never existed in the first place, freebie points are a simple and elegant solution for this, the rest should be left to roleplay, you want your character to specialize in hunting animals? Get high survival and a haven in the middle of the woods, you like to seduce your prey? Drop a few freebie points on social attributes and skills, maybe get a merit to enhance your sex appeal, you are a bagger? Streetwise/larceny and contacts etc. I also hate that I'm forced to pick a flaw at character creation, like seriously why should players be forced into more problems when compulsions and banes are already a pain in the ass? If you have a concept that fit than sure, get enemy or hunted by the SI or whatever but it should always be a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only problem here is that Freebies already carry the same problem. Giving XP would be nice, giving Flat Cost Freebies was part of the whole problem that the creation templates address in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T14:12:59-07:00","id":1482656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482654#post1482654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only problem here is that Freebies already carry the same problem. Giving XP would be nice, giving Flat Cost Freebies was part of the whole problem that the creation templates address in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I don't think that freebie points were a problem, especially with the standard xp rate of the core game but xp are fine anyway I guess, as long as the players aren't shackled by archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T14:15:53-07:00","id":1482657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482634#post1482634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would prefer to do it the way it was done in V20, you work out your flaws in game, weather they can easily solved or not, it will depend from the story, I really don't like this bargaining thing of getting something for something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't either. It make things so game-y... There are people that really are cool with the Enemy dying, but another one taking it's place? <br /> <br /> If the game aspect is more important than the story aspect, at least make things fear to the players, too. Remove santicy of merits. <br /> <br /> If my Haven 2 was burned, why I need to give a explanation to how I bought Ally 2? Like the Enemy Flaw, the Ally is part of the story now bc its writen on my sheet. I paid the refunded background points to buy another thing, and now it's part of the story. Suspend your disbelief. Done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T14:20:58-07:00","id":1482658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482295-so-predator-types?p=1482656#post1482656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think that freebie points were a problem, especially with the standard xp rate of the core game but xp are fine anyway I guess, as long as the